xmodel/block-descent-a1-rank4-dicritical-typing-d1-d4-grok46-20260831.md:1:# Source-typing lane: dicritical hypotheses (D1)--(D4)
xmodel/block-descent-a1-rank4-dicritical-typing-d1-d4-grok46-20260831.md:3:**Lane.** Bounded source-audit of the untyped bridge between Chau's dicritical *series* and Orevkov's dicritical *lines*.
xmodel/block-descent-a1-rank4-dicritical-typing-d1-d4-grok46-20260831.md:9:Throughout, a dicritical *series* is a Newton--Puiseux object `φ(x,ξ)`; a dicritical *line* (Orevkov component) is an irreducible compact curve in a regular compactification. These are not identified except where a cited source supplies a map between them.
xmodel/block-descent-a1-rank4-dicritical-typing-d1-d4-grok46-20260831.md:23:The reviewer's §5 isolates the untyped step in Lemma 2.2 of the reducible-tree ledger: Chau 2004 Lemma 1 produces a dicritical *series* `φ` and a nonconstant curve `f_φ(C)`; the next sentence replaces it by an Orevkov dicritical *line* `l ⊂ L_F` and replaces `deg f_φ > 0` by `μ_l ≥ 1`. The weakest repair named there is
xmodel/block-descent-a1-rank4-dicritical-typing-d1-d4-grok46-20260831.md:27:(D2) alpha: L_F -> Irr(A_F) is surjective;
xmodel/block-descent-a1-rank4-dicritical-typing-d1-d4-grok46-20260831.md:52:The PDF is the author-retyped AMS-TeX English text (creation date 2011-01-12). It contains Lemma 4.2, Corollary 4.3, the definitions of `L`, `L_∞`, `L_FC`, `L_C`, `L_F`, and the multiplicity used in (D3)--(D4). It does not use the word "dicritical".
