xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:13:Standing notation as in the charged report. `F=(F_1,F_2):\mathbb{A}^2\to\mathbb{A}^2` over `\mathbb{C}`; `d=[ \mathbb{C}(x,y):\mathrm{Frac}\,\mathbb{C}[F_1,F_2] ]`; `D=A_F`; `D_0=D\setminus\mathrm{Sing}\,D`; `a=\#F^{-1}(p)` for generic `p\in D_0`; `a_p=\#F^{-1}(p)`; `e_j=\mathrm{ord}_{B_j}(q^*h)`; `b=\sum_{e_j=1}\delta_j`. Compactly supported Euler characteristic `\chi_c` with `\chi_c(\mathbb{A}^n)=1`, `\chi_c(\mathrm{pt})=1`, `\chi_c(\emptyset)=0`, and closed-closed additivity.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:15:No known non-automorphism Keller map exists (that is JC), so every genuine Keller test is an automorphism (`A_F=\emptyset`, `d=1`). Non-Keller maps are used as one-hypothesis-at-a-time controls. A lemma that still holds after its stated hypothesis is dropped is recorded as using less than claimed.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:17:**Charged claims under test.** (M′) `a(\nu+s-1)-\sum_p a_p=d\nu-1` with `1\le a\le d-2`; covering `F^{-1}(D_0)\to D_0` of degree `a`; `a_p=s_p-b_p`; `e_j=1+v_j(dx\wedge dy)` for dicriticals of Keller maps; (E) `1=d\bigl(1-\chi_c(A_F)\bigr)+\chi_c(F^{-1}(A_F))`; (B-w) `\sum_j \delta_j e_j\le d-1` with some `e_j\ge 2`.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:26:**`A_F`.** Sequence `(1/n,\,cn)\to\infty` has `F=(1/n,\,c)\to(0,c)`. For `u\neq 0` the inverse is a morphism, so `F` is proper over `{u\neq 0}`. Thus `A_F=\{u=0\}\cong\mathbb{A}^1`. (This is the `v`-axis in `(u,v)`-coordinates.) Irreducible, normalisation `\mathbb{A}^1`: (H2)+(H3) hold; Keller fails.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:28:**Fibres.** Generic `p=(0,c)`, `c\neq 0`: empty, so `a=0`. At `(0,0)`: the whole `y`-axis. `F^{-1}(A_F)=\{x=0\}\cong\mathbb{A}^1`.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:34:**(B-w).** No finite `q` of degree `1` with a ramified dicritical in the report's sense. If one counts the dicritical computed in §3 (`e=1`, `\delta=1`) then `\sum\delta e=1\not\le d-1=0`. **BROKEN**, correctly, off `a\ge 1`.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:36:**Step 0 / Lemmas 2.1–2.3.** `A=\mathbb{C}[x,xy]\cong\mathbb{C}[u,v]` is integrally closed in `K`, so `B=A`, `Y\cong\mathbb{A}^2`, and `j` is `F` itself, not an open immersion. Lemma 2.1 (`A\subseteq B\subseteq\mathbb{C}[x,y]`) **HOLDS** without Keller. Lemmas 2.2–2.3 (purity of `B_Y`, `A_F=q(B_Y)` via ZMT) **BROKEN**, correctly: ZMT needs quasi-finite.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:40:### 1.2 `F=(x,y^2)` — degree 2, non-étale, proper, `A_F` empty
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:42:`Jac=2y`. Finite: `\mathbb{C}[x,y]` is a rank-2 module over `\mathbb{C}[x,y^2]`, so proper and `A_F=\emptyset`, `d=2`. Generic fibre two points; over `{v=0}` one point (ramified).
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:46:**Covering lemma / (M′) / (B-w) over `D`.** Vacuous (`D` empty). The automorphism case `F=\mathrm{id}` (Keller, `A_F=\emptyset`, `d=1`) makes (E) hold: `1=1(1-0)+0`. So emptiness of `A_F` is not itself the obstruction; ramification on `V` is.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:48:**Purity “some `e_j\ge 2` over `A_F`”.** No affine-image dicritical. The argument that the branch locus must meet `B_Y` uses étaleness on `A^2\setminus D` *and* on `U`. Here the branch locus `{y=0}` lies in `U=Y`. **Correctly inapplicable.**
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:52:`Jac=2x`, `d=2`, finite hence `A_F=\emptyset`. Restriction `U=\mathbb{A}^2\setminus\{x=0\}\to\mathbb{A}^2\setminus\{u=0\}` is étale of degree 2, non-injective (punctured-surface control). Polynomial (E) still reads `1=2`, **BROKEN** for the same reason as §1.2: ramification lives on `{x=0}\not\subset F^{-1}(A_F)=\emptyset`.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:54:If one instead computes non-properness *of the restriction* `U\to\mathbb{A}^2`, sequences `x=1/n` give `A_F(U)=\{u=0\}=q(B_Y)` with `Y=\mathbb{A}^2`, `B_Y=\{x=0\}`. Then `a=0`, one boundary point of ramification index `2` over generic `(0,c)`, and `\chi_c(U)=0=2\cdot\chi_c(\mathbb{G}_m\times\mathbb{A}^1)+0`. The identity (E) with left-hand side `1` is an `\mathbb{A}^2`-source statement; on a punctured source the same covering arithmetic holds with `\chi_c(U)` in place of `1`. **Finding:** (E) uses `source=\mathbb{A}^2` for the constant `1`, not merely étaleness.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:56:### 1.4 `F=(x,\,y+xy^2)` — quasi-finite, non-proper, Keller fails only off `V` in a weaker sense
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:60:**`A_F`.** Set `x_n=(b-y_n)/y_n^2` with `y_n\to\infty`: then `u_n\to 0` and `v_n\to b`. For `u` bounded away from `0` the quadratic inverse stays finite on compacts. Thus `A_F=\{u=0\}\cong\mathbb{A}^1`, (H2)+(H3) hold.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:62:**Fibres over `D`.** `{x=0\}\xrightarrow{\sim}\{u=0\}`: `a=1=a_p` for all `p\in D`. Interior ramification remains: discriminant `{1+4uv=0\}\subset V=\mathbb{A}^2\setminus D`. So `F` is *not* étale on all of `V`, hence not Keller, but it *is* quasi-finite and `A_F` is a line.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:68:**(B-w) “some `e_j\ge 2`”.** Over `D` one has `e=1`, `b=1`, `d=a+b=2`, no ramified dicritical. Branch locus is the discriminant, not `A_F`. **BROKEN**, correctly, off Keller. The inequality `\sum\delta_j e_j=1\le d-1=1` still holds.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:70:**(M′) with `\nu=s=0`.** `-a=-1`, so `a=1`. Holds numerically (see §2). The smooth-`A_F` law `a=1` therefore **HOLDS** on a non-Keller quasi-finite map.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:72:### 1.5 Automorphisms (Keller, `A_F` empty) and proper maps with `A_F` empty
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:74:`F=\mathrm{id}`: Keller, `d=1`, `A_F=\emptyset`. (E) holds. (M′)/(H2) inapplicable. Prop. 2.5 (`d\ge 3`) uses a branch component of `A_F`; correctly silent.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:76:`F=(x^2,y^2)`: `Jac=4xy`, finite, `d=4`, `A_F=\emptyset`. (E) says `1=4`, **BROKEN**. Same mechanism as §1.2.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:88:**Findings.** (i) The covering lemma and the smooth-`A_F` evaluation of (M′) use quasi-finiteness plus the topology of `D_0`, not the full Keller package. (ii) The ceiling `a\le d-2` and “some `e_j\ge 2`” use Keller on `V` essentially; `F=(x,y+xy^2)` is the explicit `a=d-1` control. (iii) (E) as written uses étaleness on `V` *or* else `\chi_c(V)=0` (accidental vanishing); the latter is why (E) survives on `(x,xy)` and `(x,y+xy^2)`.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:93:Theorem 5.2 claims `1=d\bigl(1-\chi_c(A_F)\bigr)+\chi_c(F^{-1}(A_F))` for Keller maps, via `F^{-1}(V)\to V` a degree-`d` covering and 5.1(a)–(b).
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:97:`A_F\cong\mathbb{A}^1`, `\chi_c=1`. `F^{-1}(A_F)\cong\mathbb{A}^1`, `\chi_c=1`. `d=1`. RHS `=1(1-1)+1=1`. **HOLDS.**
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:105:`A_F=\emptyset`, `\chi_c=0`. `F^{-1}(\emptyset)=\emptyset`, `\chi_c=0`. `d=2`. RHS `=2`. **BROKEN** (`1\neq 2`). Directly: `\chi_c(\mathbb{A}^2)=1\neq 2\cdot\chi_c(\mathbb{A}^2)`. Hypothesis that fails: unramified covering over `V=\mathbb{A}^2`.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:109:`A_F\cong\mathbb{A}^1`, `\chi_c=1`. `F^{-1}(A_F)\cong\mathbb{A}^1`, `\chi_c=1`. `d=2`. RHS `=2\cdot 0+1=1`. **HOLDS.**
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:111:Here `F^{-1}(V)\to V` is *ramified* (discriminant `{1+4uv=0\}`). Multiplicativity is not licensed, yet both sides of `\chi_c(F^{-1}(V))=d\,\chi_c(V)` are `0=2\cdot 0`. **Finding:** (E) is not probed by any control with `\chi_c(A_F)=1`, because the coefficient of `d` vanishes. The only desk control with `\chi_c(A_F)\neq 1` is `A_F=\emptyset` (`\chi_c=0`), where (E) *does* break off Keller.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:113:An affine nodal cubic would give `\chi_c(D)=0` by 5.1(c) (`D^\sim\cong\mathbb{A}^1`, one node, `r_p=2`, `\chi_c=1-1=0`), hence (E) would read `\chi_c(F^{-1}(D))=1-d`. No explicit polynomial `F` with `A_F` a nodal cubic was constructed at desk. **UNTESTABLE-AT-DESK** for singular `A_F` with `\chi_c\neq 1`.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:123:On Keller automorphisms: **HOLDS** (both sides `1`). On the two non-Keller controls with `A_F\cong\mathbb{A}^1`: **HOLDS**, because étaleness is used only over `V` *or* `\chi_c(V)=0`. On proper ramified maps with `A_F=\emptyset`: **BROKEN**, and this is the only desk probe of the factor `d`. The proof uses less than “Keller on all of `\mathbb{A}^2`”: it uses a degree-`d` unramified covering over `V=\mathbb{A}^2\setminus A_F` plus `\chi_c(\mathrm{source})=1`.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:155:Second blowup `s=\alpha`, `t=\alpha\beta`: `F` becomes `[\alpha\beta:1:\beta]` in the first chart of §1.1's homogeneous form, i.e. affine `(u,v)=(\alpha,1/\beta)` for `\beta\neq 0,\infty`. Restriction to `E_2=\{\alpha=0\}` is non-constant onto `{u=0\}=\overline{A_F}`: this is the dicritical. Also `dx\wedge dy=-d\alpha\wedge d\beta/(\alpha\beta^2)`, so `v_{E_2}=-1`, matching the free two-blowup.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:165:From §1.4, `A_F=\{u=0\}`, `e=1` (isomorphism over `D`), `Jac=1+2xy`. Escaping sequences have `x\sim -1/y`, so `1+2xy\to -1` and `v(Jac)=0` along the dicritical.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:169:**Finding.** Lemma 4.2's local proof gives `e=1+v(Jac)+v(dx\wedge dy)` without Keller; Keller is used only to set `v(Jac)=0` (a nonzero constant has valuation `0` at every place). The formula can hold off Keller (`F=(x,y+xy^2)`) and can fail off Keller (`F=(x,xy)`). The existence of a valuation at infinity with `v(dx\wedge dy)=0` is not merely abstract: it is realised as a dicritical of an explicit quasi-finite polynomial map. Closing box `(Y\setminus U,\,e=1)` therefore cannot be a purely valuative prohibition; the report's OPEN at `d=4` transposition class is consistent with this control.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:185:- `(1,2)`: one dicritical, `b=0`.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:192:- One dicritical: `(1,3)` (`e=3\ge 2`, `b=0`); `(3,1)` forbidden.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:193:- Two dicriticals: `(1,2)+(1,1)` (has `e=2`, `b=1`); `(2,1)+(1,1)` all `e=1`, forbidden.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:262:On `F=(x,y+xy^2)` this is visible: `q^{-1}(D)` has two components over `D\cong\mathbb{A}^1` (simply connected, covering trivial), one in `U` (the line `{x=0\}`) and one in `B_Y` (the `v=0` dicritical of §3.3), neither mixed. The affine line `{x=0\}` is already closed in `U`; its compactification meets the dicritical, but that meeting is at infinity of `Y`, not over `D_0`. **Confirms** Lemma 3.3.
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:264:On `F=(x,xy)` the `y`-axis *does* escape to the dicritical over the origin, a smooth point of `D`. Mixed/escaping over `D_0`. But `q` is not finite, `j` is not an open immersion (§1.1). **BROKEN only off the hypotheses.**
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:281:| (E) as a Keller theorem | **HOLDS** on automorphisms; **BROKEN** off Keller when `\chi_c(V)\neq 0` (`F=(x,y^2)`, `1\neq 2`); **HOLDS** off Keller when `\chi_c(A_F)=1` (`(x,xy)`, `(x,y+xy^2)`) | Factor `d` untested except on `A_F=\emptyset`. Singular `A_F` with `\chi_c\neq 1`: **UNTESTABLE-AT-DESK**. Proof uses a covering over `V` plus `\chi_c(\mathbb{A}^2)=1`, less than global Keller. |
xmodel/round1033-sheet-gate-verification-grok46-20260831.md:287:| Lemma 4.2, `e=1+v(dx\wedge dy)` | **HOLDS** as local algebra with the Jac term. Keller form: **BROKEN** on `(x,xy)` (`1+v=0\neq e=1`); **HOLDS** on `(x,y+xy^2)` (`v=0=e-1`) | `v=-3,-2,-1,-4` as computed; `v=0` exists (three free blowups) and is dicritical for a quasi-finite map. OPEN at `d=4` is consistent. |
