xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:53:5. **The one-cusp quartic horn is a saturated two-curve problem whose residual Kummer class is inverse.** Integration `2531a89d...` saturates Orevkov--Chau and forces a companion `A1` self-identification. Successor `bcc5148...` kills the independent-Kummer shortcut: `[E]=-[Phi]`, the collision is a monogenic index locus `u^mu-v^mu=0`, and Formanek makes the ruling coordinate primitive in the quartic field. No second ruling, no ramification of `pi`, and no `mu^2 | d1` follow.
xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:70:| 6 | Abhyankar–Moh one-place | **reopen** | The classical category error (fibres are multi-place) is now avoided: Chau plus the all-degree theorem put the one-place theorem on cyclic components of `A(F)`. This is a genuine revival, not a slogan. |
xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:216:2. **Reducible `B`.** Chau still makes each component one-place, but `K_infty` is a link. Then `|H1(Sigma_2)|` need not be finite, `det` is a link determinant, and (3.2) as written is meaningless. The minimal rank-four row with two components meeting at the unique `(2,2)` point is a 2-component link at infinity. That is a different, still open, cell.
xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:248:**Index-at-infinity.** `Disc(P_t)=2 I_t` on `V=A2-B`. The coincidence divisor is supported on `I_t`. Orevkov--Chau is saturated, so a single positive boundary packet from `I_t` kills the horn. The missing theorem must charge `I_t` as normalization index of the monogenic order `O(V)[t]`, **not** as ramification of the etale normalization and **not** as a nonproper component of `H`. This is the same typing firewall that `DISC8-INDEX` already promoted for rank-three algebras (source different, target discriminant, reduced branch, Fitting/length index are four objects). Reuse that dictionary; do not rebuild it. Idea F is the cross-avenue form.
xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:282:**Required hypotheses.** Charged one-place Chau parametrization; goodness and `G_infty ->> G_aff` (Opus-provisional); simple connected monodromy; irreducibility of `B`. Do not charge a proper block: the statement is cover-theoretic.
xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:294:**Hoped-for implication.** The coincidence divisor `I_t` contributes at least one Orevkov--Chau boundary unit. Saturation of `4mu-1 = 2mu r + 2mu - 1` then contradicts the one-cusp horn.
xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:328:**Primary theorem interface.** Kummer sequence (4.1) and nodal computation (5.1)--(5.3) of `f5dbad98...`; Chau polynomial parametrization.
xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:336:**Hoped-for implication.** A cyclic one-place component of `A(F)` cannot be a coordinate (it has a cycle, so it is not a line). Abhyankar--Moh plus the semigroup of a one-place rational curve constrain the embedding dimension and the generators of the value semigroup. Combined with the knot-type list of Section 3, this may force the component to have embedding degree incompatible with being a nonproper-value curve of a Keller map (Chau's polynomial parametrization has to be a Keller-asymptotic, not an arbitrary polynomial curve).
xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:338:**Required hypotheses.** Promoted all-degree cycle theorem; Chau Theorem 1 / Corollary 2 as pinned in `9579d3a1...`; Abhyankar--Moh only after the curve is known to be one-place, which it is. Do not apply AM to fibres of `(F,G)`. Do not conclude that `A(F)` is a line.
xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:342:**Primary theorem interface.** Chau 2004, Theorem 1; Abhyankar--Moh embedding theorem; Orevkov--Chau budget; Neumann characteristic Puiseux pairs.
