xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:54:## 2. Dicritical divisors and non-properness sets (post-2020)
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:56:Target: post-2020 dicriticals of polynomial maps \(\mathbb{A}^2\to\mathbb{A}^2\), Jelonek non-properness sets, Domrina–Orevkov-style low-degree classifications. Bearing on `OPEN[RESIDUAL-TO-DOMRINA-STATE]` and the one-cusp horn (local dicritical picture at infinity).
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:58:**F11. Corral–Gómez-Martínez–Senovilla-Sanz, *Cuspidal dicritical foliations and analytical invariants of cusps*, arXiv:2605.30634v1, 2026-05-28.** SHA-256 `d3bc4da7093756084cada50f9eb0a90344d9108aae488454fcb42b999e176cd1`. Local germs of foliations on \((\mathbb{C}^2,0)\): a foliation is *cuspidal dicritical* if after the minimal resolution of a cusp it is totally \(E\)-dicritical along the cuspidal divisor. The invariant curves through free points of \(E\) are equisingular cusps, not in general analytically equivalent. Main theorems: \(\ell\)-transversality with a minimal standard basis of 1-forms freezes the first \(\ell+2\) generators of the semimodule \(\Lambda_C\) of differential values; a bound on the divisorial value \(\nu_E(\omega_{\mathcal{F}})\) in terms of the conductor of \(\Lambda_C\) forces \(\Lambda\)-constancy of the whole family. Explicit conductor formula \(c(\Lambda_C)=\tilde u_{s+1}-n-m+1\). **STRUCTURE** for the local analytic classification of one-Puiseux-pair branches and for the vocabulary “dicritical along a cusp.” **IRRELEVANT** as a close of Domrina–Orevkov or of a global polynomial Keller map: these are local foliations, not polynomial self-maps of \(\mathbb{A}^2\), and the Jacobian of a Keller map is a *constant*, not a foliation 1-form.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:60:**F12. Artal Bartolo–Veys, *Dicritical divisors and hypercurvettes*, arXiv:2505.24648v1 (hashed 2026-09-01 `cdbb75f8…`).** Local existence of prescribed dicriticals in dim \(\ge 3\). Already registered. **STRUCTURE** for the word; **IRRELEVANT** to global plane Keller dicriticals.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:62:**F13. El Hilany survey 2501.03828v2 and tropical non-properness 2207.00989v2.** Already registered 2026-09-01. **STRUCTURE** for \(A_F\) as a Jelonek set.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:64:No post-2020 source found that produces, or forbids, a \(\mu=1\) affine-image dicritical for an irreducible-\(A_F\) plane Keller map, or that repairs/extends Domrina I–II / Domrina–Orevkov beyond the campaign’s own replays. Orevkov’s 2025–2026 papers are germs ramified over \(u^{d_1}=v^{d_2}\) (F14), a degree-10 triple-point construction (F25), and real-quartic arrangements relative to three lines (arXiv:2607.19457v2, SHA-256 `6f225cbf8f682d28af1f6d3736d005044f3dbd0f2670ef70440bc7846e7eecdb`, **IRRELEVANT**), not a low-degree Keller classification. **`OPEN[RESIDUAL-TO-DOMRINA-STATE]` stands.**
