xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-grok46.md:86:5. **Degree-monotone invariant, if one exists.** Adjacent colourable survivors at conductors 12/14/18/20/24/26 are a promoted existence proof that the ladder is not monotone. A new invariant must come from algebra (semigroup, residual cover, dicritical remainder), not from more even conductors.
xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-grok46.md:110:**Setup, from promoted facts only.** An actual rank-four proper block has irreducible reduced charged branch `B`, `normalization(B)=A1`, and generic branch partition `(2,1,1)` or `(3,1)` with one ramification point (`H_inertia` at `5d7df7ce…:84–104`, consumed by the `m=1` integration). So a generic point of `B subset A_F` has fibre cycle type either one 2-cycle plus two 1-cycles, or one 3-cycle plus one 1-cycle. Write `B^sm` for the smooth locus of `B`. The unique ramified preimage along generic `B` is the ramified sheet. The complementary preimages form an unramified covering `Sigma -> B^sm` of degree 2 in the `(2,1,1)` case and degree 1 in the `(3,1)` case. These are *sheets of the finite map*, not dicritical divisors and not flags of a compactification. Flag/place/series: this covering is not identified with an Orevkov dicritical, nor with a physical place of `B`, nor with the cover series of a splice diagram.
xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-grok46.md:114:- `(3,1)`: degree 1, so a section of `F` over `B^sm`. A holomorphic section of a nonproper map along its nonproper-value curve cannot extend to a proper section over all of `B` (that would split `F` over `B` and contradict that `B` consists of nonproper values: Chau 2003, `A_F` is the union of images of dicritical series). The obstruction is therefore *extension across the affine singularities and across infinity*. If the section extends through every affine singularity, `B` would carry a polynomial right-inverse on a Zariski-open of itself; that is a coordinate-recognition statement on the unique `A_F` component, i.e. a correctly typed Abhyankar–Moh client (row 6), not the old multi-place fibre abuse. If it cannot extend, the obstruction is supported at the singularities and is therefore a function of the δ-sequence / conductor of `B`.
xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-grok46.md:115:- `(2,1,1)`: degree 2, either two sections or a connected étale double cover of `B^sm`. Two sections reduce to the `(3,1)` extension problem with multiplicity two. A connected double cover of `A1 minus s` punctures is classified by the subset of punctures of odd ramification (plus possibly infinity). The numerical semigroup of a one-place curve determines those punctures (Assi–García-Sánchez, arXiv:1407.0490: a δ-sequence determines the semigroup, the conductor, and the affine singularities). A colourable survivor whose semigroup cannot carry either two sections or such a double cover is combinatorially unrealizable as `A_F`, even though it is colourable as a braid. Which of the two topologies occurs is `OPEN` until typed; do not fill by cap.
xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-grok46.md:119:**Primary literature.** Chau, *Two remarks on non-zero constant Jacobian polynomial maps of `C^2`*, Ann. Polon. Math. 82.1 (2003), Lemma 5: `A_F` equals the union of images of dicritical series. Orevkov 1987, (4) and Cor. 4.3, used only as already typed at plane rank four (no export). Assi–García-Sánchez, *Algorithms for curves with one place at infinity*, J. Symbolic Comput. / arXiv:1407.0490, for the semigroup-to-punctures dictionary. Galindo–Monserrat–Moreno-Ávila–Moyano-Fernández, *On δ-sequences and surfaces at infinity*, arXiv:2408.15931, for the dual graph of the resolution at infinity from a δ-sequence. Neumann–Rudolph unfolding and Neumann's minimal-Seifert theorem as already consumed by the promoted one-node packet (C1 mandatory).
xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-grok46.md:121:**What it is not.** It is not a claim that `m=1` holds at every degree. It is not an identification of the residual cover with a dicritical. If the extension obstruction cannot be typed, the output is `OPEN`, not a cap.
xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-grok46.md:127:Rows involved: **#2** (dicritical / Eggers–Wall / Orevkov budget), **#27** (splice / δ-diagram of the unique `B`), **#6/#7** (one-place `A(F)`), and the one-cusp valuation table (not itself a numbered row; it is the live client of **#29** after LND died).
xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-grok46.md:129:**The identification that is licensed.** At rank four, `m=1` plus (D2) (dicriticals surject onto `Irr(A_F)`) implies every Orevkov dicritical maps to the same unique curve `B`. Orevkov 1987 formula (4) gives
xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-grok46.md:133:with each inner summand nonnegative (Cor. 4.3). Theorem 10.1 plus `H_inertia` charges at least one owner dicritical with `mu >= 2`. The *remainder* `3 - mu_owner` is therefore in `{0,1}` and is a numerical invariant of the unique branch. Domrina–Orevkov (one dicritical component) and Domrina, Izv. Math. 64 (2000) (two dicritical components) already classified the number of *dicritical compactification components* for `N=4`; that number is 1 or 2 and is *not* `m`. Flag/place/series: dicritical component, `A_F` component, and cover-cycle type stay distinct. The remainder is a count of multiplicities on compactification divisors mapping onto `B`, not a count of places of `B`.
xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-grok46.md:135:**The identification that is new.** The one-cusp partition table's discriminator is `Theta_h = d_h - r_h - 2`, with `gamma_h = Theta_h / 2` required to be an integer for the row to exist. Here `d_h` is the mapping degree of a horizontal (dicritical) boundary component and `r_h` is its residual intersection count with the rest of the boundary. That is the same numerical species as `(mu_l, corrections)` in Orevkov's inner sum: `mu_l` is a mapping degree on a dicritical, and the correction terms are excess intersection/ramification along `pi(l)`. For the unique rank-four `B`, the remainder `{0,1}` is therefore a *parity and size constraint on `Theta_h` of every dicritical mapping to `B`*, and conversely a one-cusp SNC computation of `(d_h, r_h)` is a computation of the Orevkov remainder in the special case where the compactification is the one-cusp ring.
xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-grok46.md:141:- Row 25's colouring census and row 2's dicritical budget, which the 2026-08-21 surveys treated as one “sheet-number ladder,” are now *separated*: colouring is saturated as a genus-killer; the budget remainder is not.
xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-grok46.md:229:**Dependencies.** Promoted `m=1`; promoted `H_inertia` (generic partition `(2,1,1)` or `(3,1)`, one ramification point, `normalization(B)=A1`); conjugacy sentence C1 of the one-node packet (mandatory in citations, harvest §4); Chau 2003 Lemma 5 (`A_F` = images of dicritical series); Assi–García-Sánchez δ-sequence dictionary. Does *not* depend on (2.3), Prop. 4.3, C3, inverse-Kummer, or any reducible-row lemma.
xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-grok46.md:235:- `(3,1)` section extends through all affine singularities: this is a correctly typed AM/coordinate-recognition client on unique `A_F`. Either `B` is a coordinate value (contradicting nonproperness of an actual block) or the extension produces an explicit polynomial right-inverse along `B` that can be checked against `J=1`. Either way the `(3,1)` horn dies or yields a map. Information: high.
xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-grok46.md:237:- `(2,1,1)` residual exists as neither two sections nor a connected double cover: that δ-sequence is combinatorially unrealizable as `A_F`. Kill the row. This is attainment, not colouring.
xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-grok46.md:247:**Dependencies.** Card-independent of Card I. Promoted `m=1`; Orevkov 1987 (4) and Cor. 4.3 at the already-typed plane rank-four scope (no export); `mu_owner >= 2` from Theorem 10.1 + `H_inertia`; Domrina–Orevkov / Domrina 2000 only as a reminder that the number of dicritical *compactification* components for `N=4` is 1 or 2, not as a source of `m`; Galindo et al. arXiv:2408.15931 for dual graphs from δ-sequences; the fail-closed calculator of §6. Does not consume the quarantined 16-row ledger, R1 census, or winding-two residue theorem on satellite companions (wave-2/3 §1: never apply that theorem to satellite companions).
xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-grok46.md:249:**Cheapest discriminator.** For the shortest colourable surviving δ-sequence (lowest `Delta_aff` among `{6,7,9,10,…}` that the ladder lists as colourable), build its resolution-at-infinity dual graph from the δ-sequence combinatorics. Ask whether the graph admits a horizontal vertex of mapping degree `mu in {2,3}` with remainder `3-mu in {0,1}`. Three admissible remainder types, and only these: one dicritical with `mu=3` and zero correction; one with `mu=2` and correction 1; one with `mu=2` plus a second dicritical with `mu=1` mapping to the same `B`. Type `(1+1+1)` is forbidden by `mu_owner >= 2`. The calculator of §6 is the discriminator; a hand table with the same branches is acceptable.
