+equations force `x=0`, `y=0`.  Thus `a_{p_0}=1`, `r_{p_0}=1`, and MPRIME's
+fibre law gives
+
+```text
+K_{p_0} = N - a_{p_0} - r_{p_0} W = 6 - 1 - 2 = 3 = a - 1.
+```
+
+There are no other affine singularities of `A_F`, so `(K)` is matched exactly.
